From 11eee48da2b117a2c0aafb2d71c50b0104b7d1fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=E4=BB=93=E9=BC=A0=E7=8E=8B?= <yjianbin419@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:02:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ORD-0361: a map marker becomes a control, and the pick is
 remembered per journey

Tapping a stop produced no observable consequence: the markers were plain divs with an aria-label
and no handler anywhere in the panel, so the map was a picture you could drag. Markers now answer a
tap, Enter and Space; an unpickable one says why in the traveller's words with the contract field
that decided it named beside the sentence; and the picked stop is kept in a journey-scoped entry
alongside the shell's other citynexus.v8.* keys, so re-entering the page restores it. The rail's
rows became focusable cards that scroll into view and take focus for the picked stop.

Not claimed: at this generation the map and the per-stop rail are on different tabs (MapPanel at
V8Experience.tsx:2918/3497/3702, the rail inside AuthoritativeExecution), so the scroll-and-focus
half has no screen where it can fire. That pairing is a product decision, not something to fake
with a stand-in list.
